{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975787,"nonce":"pzGwRroYI2vCodgUMpr9gHN7FtU=","title":"Tail-recursion elimination refuses cell parameters","message":"Rather than writing through the cell: a pinned argument register is a memory slot\nwhose address may have escaped, and each real activation gets a fresh one.\nNarrowing this to `Ref`-taken parameters only would let `Incr`/`Decr` counters\nthrough. It also refuses when a non-argument `Param` is still read, for the same\nreason SROA refuses a read-before-write. Mutual recursion is out of scope.","files":null}]}